    descriptionEn: `I must note an inconsistency in the provided data: 'Belgian Death Metal' doesn't correspond to the mentioned artists (Metallica, Iron Maiden, Black Sabbath), who belong to traditional heavy metal and thrash metal, not Belgian death metal.

Authentic Belgian death metal emerged in the early 1990s, primarily around Brussels and Antwerp. The term combines 'death metal' (referencing the genre's mortality themes) with Belgian geographical origin. Influenced by Floridian death metal (Death, Morbid Angel) and British grindcore (Napalm Death), this movement developed a distinctive technical approach.

Emblemmatic bands like Agathocles and Leng Tch'e employ drop-tuned guitars (Gibson Flying V, ESP with active EMG pickups), double-kick drum kits (Pearl, Tama), and extreme guttural vocals. Tempos range from 180-250 BPM, featuring complex time signatures (7/8, 5/4) and characteristic blast beats.

This genre reflects Belgian underground counter-culture, expressing sharp social criticism through lyrics addressing social injustice and urban alienation, particularly within the post-industrial Walloon context. The scene's DIY ethos and anti-establishment stance resonated with Belgium's politically fragmented landscape, creating a unique European death metal identity distinct from Scandinavian or American variants.`,
